                                                                                                         ]
                                                                                                       ) ;
                                                                                    rdf:type owl:Class
                                                                                  ]
                                                             ] ;
                                             rdfs:label "Electrochemical Impedance Spectroscopy"@en ;
                                             skos:definition "Electrochemical Impedance Spectroscopy (EIS) is a technique that measures the frequency-dependent complex impedance of an electrochemical system by applying a small sinusoidal voltage perturbation over a range of frequencies to characterize electrode kinetics, diffusion, and double-layer capacitance."@en ;
                                             pmdco:abbreviation "EIS"@en ;
                                             pmdco:definitionSource "claude-sonnet-4-6"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/CHIPS/metrology-ontology/Electrochemical_Mass_Spectrometry
chips:Electrochemical_Mass_Spectrometry rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                        rdfs:subClassOf chips:Mass_Spectrometry ;
                                        rdfs:label "Electrochemical Mass Spectrometry"@en ;
                                        skos:definition "Electrochemical Mass Spectrometry is a technique that couples an electrochemical cell with a mass spectrometer to identify and quantify gaseous reaction products evolved at an electrode surface during electrochemical processes."@en ;
                                        pmdco:abbreviation "EC-MS"@en ;
                                        pmdco:definitionSource "claude-sonnet-4-6"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/CHIPS/metrology-ontology/Electrochemical_Scanning_Tunneling_Microscopy
