                        dcterms:bibliographicCitation "National Institute of Standards and Technology. (2022). Strategic Opportunities for U.S. Semiconductor Manufacturing: Facilitating U.S. Leadership and Competitiveness through Advancements in Measurements and Standards (NIST Special Publication CHIPS 1000). U.S. Department of Commerce."@en ;
                        dcterms:title "Metrology for Materials Purity, Properties and Provenance"@en ;
                        rdfs:label "Grand Challenge 1"@en ;
                        rdfs:seeAlso "https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/CHIPS/NIST.CHIPS.1000.pdf" ;
                        skos:definition "Develop measurement technologies, properties data, and standards focused on defect and contaminant identification . The objective is to support uniform materials quality across suppliers and to enable tracking of potential sources of impurity."@en ;
                        pmdco:abbreviation "GC 1" .


