                              skos:definition "High-harmonic Generation is a nonlinear optical process in which a medium driven by an intense laser field emits coherent radiation at integer multiples of the fundamental photon energy, producing attosecond pulses and coherent extreme-ultraviolet or soft X-ray beams for ultrafast spectroscopy."@en ;
                              pmdco:abbreviation "HHG"@en ;
                              pmdco:definitionSource "claude-sonnet-4-6"@en .


