                                      rdfs:label "High-resolution X-ray Diffraction"@en ;
                                      skos:definition "High-Resolution X-ray Diffraction (HRXRD) is an X-ray diffraction technique that uses a crystal monochromator and analyzer to achieve very high angular resolution, enabling measurement of lattice mismatch, strain, and composition in epitaxial thin films."@en ;
                                      pmdco:definitionSource "claude-sonnet-4-6"@en ;
                                      pmdco:symbol "HRXRD" .


