                 skos:definition "A nanosecond is a unit of time equal to 10⁻⁹ seconds, relevant to transistor switching speed, time-of-flight measurements, and fast transient characterization."@en ;
                 pmdco:definitionSource "claude-sonnet-4-6"@en .


