                    skos:definition "Scatterometry is an optical metrology technique that determines the geometry, critical dimensions, and overlay of sub-wavelength periodic structures by measuring the intensity or phase of diffracted light as a function of angle or wavelength."@en ;
                    pmdco:definitionSource "claude-sonnet-4-6"@en .


