                                  skos:definition "Spin-Polarized Electron Beam is an electron beam in which the spin angular momentum of electrons is aligned along a preferred axis, used in spin-polarized LEEM, PEEM, and electron scattering experiments."@en ;
                                  pmdco:definitionSource "claude-sonnet-4-6"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/CHIPS/metrology-ontology/Spinpolarized_Neutron_Beam
