                           skos:definition "Thermal Spectroscopy is a spectroscopic technique that uses thermally induced carrier emission or optical excitation as a function of temperature to probe the energy levels of defects and traps in semiconductor materials."@en ;
                           pmdco:definitionSource "claude-sonnet-4-6"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/CHIPS/metrology-ontology/Thermalization_Map
