                               skos:definition "X-ray Computed Tomography (CT) is a tomographic imaging process that acquires X-ray transmission projections from multiple angles around a specimen and reconstructs a three-dimensional volumetric image of internal structure."@en ;
                               pmdco:abbreviation "XCT"@en ;
                               pmdco:definitionSource "claude-sonnet-4-6"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/CHIPS/metrology-ontology/Xray_Computed_Tomography_System
chips:Xray_Computed_Tomography_System rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                      rdfs:subClassOf mo:Optisches_Mikroskop ,
