                                                                                        )
                                                                          ]
                                                     ] ;
                                     rdfs:label "X-ray Fluorescence Spectroscopy"@en ;
                                     skos:definition "X-ray Fluorescence Spectroscopy (XRF) is an elemental analysis technique that irradiates a specimen with primary X-rays to eject inner-shell electrons, and the characteristic secondary X-ray fluorescence emitted upon electron relaxation identifies and quantifies elements non-destructively."@en ;
                                     pmdco:abbreviation "XRF" ;
                                     pmdco:definitionSource "claude-sonnet-4-6"@en .


