###  https://w3id.org/pmd/mo/Anode
mo:Anode rdf:type owl:Class ;
         rdfs:subClassOf mo:Elektrode ;
         rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/pmd/mo> ;
         rdfs:label "Anode"@de ,
                    "Anode"@en ;
         skos:definition "The anode is the positively charged electrode in an electrochemical cell or other electrically driven systems. It serves as the site where oxidation occurs, meaning electrons are released from the anode, typically moving towards the cathode. In devices like batteries, the anode is where electrons are produced during the discharge process."@en ;
         pmdco:definitionSource "ChatGPT 3.5"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/mo/Atmosphrische_Rasterelektronenmikroskopie
mo:Atmosphrische_Rasterelektronenmikroskopie rdf:type owl:Class ;
