                      skos:definition "A Field Emission Gun is an electron gun used in electron microscopes to produce an electron beam with extremely high brightness and coherence. It relies on the phenomenon of field emission, where electrons are emitted from a sharp emitter tip under the influence of a strong electric field. FEGs are capable of producing highly focused electron beams, leading to enhanced imaging resolution and analytical capabilities."@en ;
