                  rdfs:label "Condensor Lens"@en ,
                             "Kondensorlinse"@de ;
                  skos:altLabel "Condensor Lens"@en ,
                                "Kondensorlinse"@de ;
                  skos:definition "A condenser lens is an optical element used in microscopy and other optical systems to focus and control the illumination on the sample being observed. It is positioned below the light source and directs light rays onto the specimen, making the illumination uniform and optimizing the quality of the sample's image. The condenser lens helps enhance contrast, resolution, and overall image quality by ensuring that a consistent and concentrated light beam illuminates the specimen."@en ;
                  pmdco:definitionSource "ChatGPT 3.5"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/mo/Konfokale_LaserScanningMikroskopie
mo:Konfokale_LaserScanningMikroskopie rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                      rdfs:subClassOf pmdco:Optische_Mikroskopie ,
                                                      [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                        owl:onProperty prov:wasAssociatedWith ;
                                                        owl:someValuesFrom chips:Laser_Scanning_Confocal_Light_Microscope
                                                      ] ;
                                      rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/pmd/mo> ;
                                      rdfs:label "Confocal Laser Scanning Microscopy"@en ,
                                                 "Konfokale Laser-Scanning-Mikroskopie"@de ;
                                      skos:definition "Confocal Laser Scanning Microscopy (CLSM) is an optical imaging technique that enhances resolution and eliminates out-of-focus blur by using a spatial pinhole and laser illumination. A focused laser beam is scanned across the sample's surface or depth, and only the light emitted from the focal plane (or a defined section) passes through the pinhole to form an image. CLSM provides high-resolution three-dimensional images, making it popular for biological imaging and studying fluorescently labeled samples."@en ;
                                      pmdco:definitionSource "ChatGPT 3.5"@en ;
                                      mo:abbreviation "CLSM"@en .


