###  https://w3id.org/pmd/mo/Winkel
mo:Winkel rdf:type owl:Class ;
          rdfs:subClassOf chips:Quantity_Kind ,
                          chips:Spatial_Concept ;
          rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/mo> ,
                     "Angle [Geometric]"@en ,
                     "Winkel"@de ;
          skos:definition """In der Geometrie und Trigonometrie ist ein Winkel ein Maß für eine Drehung, das erforderlich ist, um eine Linie oder Ebene mit einer anderen zur Deckung zu bringen. Ein Winkel wird durch zwei Strahlen gebildet, die einen gemeinsamen Endpunkt haben, der als Scheitelpunkt des Winkels bezeichnet wird. Die Strahlen werden als die Seiten des Winkels bezeichnet. 

Hinweis: Das Konzept des Winkels ist in der Geometrie von grundlegender Bedeutung und wird häufig verwendet, um die relative Ausrichtung von Linien, Ebenen oder Flächen zu beschreiben. Winkel werden in der Regel in Grad (°) oder Bogenmaß (rad) gemessen."""@de ,
                          """In geometry and trigonometry, an angle is a measure of the amount of rotation needed to bring one line or plane into coincidence with another. An angle is formed by two rays that share a common endpoint, known as the vertex of the angle. The rays are referred to as the sides of the angle. 

Note: The concept of an angle is fundamental in geometry and is often used to describe the relative orientation of lines, planes, or surfaces. Angles are typically measured in degrees (°) or radians (rad)."""@en ;
          pmdco:definitionSource "ChatGPT 3.5"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/mo/Working_Distance
mo:Working_Distance rdf:type owl:Class ;
                    rdfs:subClassOf pmdco:Abstand ;
                    rdfs:comment "Der Arbeitsabstand wirkt sich auf die Tiefenschärfe und die Auflösung des Bildes aus."@de ,
                                 "The working distance affects the depth of field and the resolution of the image."@en ;
                    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/pmd/mo> ;
                    rdfs:label "Arbeitsabstand"@de ,
                               "Working Distance"@en ;
                    skos:definition "Der Abstand zwischen der Objektivlinse des Elektronenmikroskops und der Probenoberfläche, wenn der Elektronenstrahl auf die Probe fokussiert wird."@de ,
                                    "The distance between the electron microscope objective lens and the specimen surface when the electron beam is focused on the specimen."@en ;
                    pmdco:definitionSource "ChatGPT 3.5" .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/mo/Xray_Absorption_Near_Edge_Spectroscopy
mo:Xray_Absorption_Near_Edge_Spectroscopy rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                          rdfs:subClassOf chips:Xray_Spectroscopy ,
                                                          [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                            owl:onProperty chips:measured ;
                                                            owl:someValuesFrom chips:Oxidation_State
                                                          ] ,
                                                          [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                            owl:onProperty pmdco:belongsToProject ;
                                                            owl:someValuesFrom chips:Grand_Challenge_7
                                                          ] ;
                                          rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/pmd/mo> ;
                                          rdfs:label "Röntgenabsorptionsspektroskopie im Nahbereich"@de ,
                                                     "X-ray Absorption Near Edge Spectroscopy"@en ;
                                          skos:definition """X-ray Absorption Near Edge Spectroscopy (XANES) is a specialized technique used in the field of materials science and spectroscopy to study the electronic and structural properties of materials. It focuses on the X-ray absorption spectra of atoms within a sample, particularly the region just above the absorption edge of an element's X-ray absorption spectrum.
In XANES, a sample is irradiated with X-rays, typically generated by a synchrotron radiation source. These X-rays are tuned to specific energy levels corresponding to the absorption edges of the elements of interest in the sample. As the X-rays are absorbed by the sample, the energy levels of the atoms are altered, leading to various transitions in their electron configurations. The resulting X-ray absorption spectrum is measured, specifically targeting the energies just above the absorption edge.
XANES provides information about the electronic structure of the atoms within the sample, including the oxidation state, chemical bonding, and local environment of the absorbing element. The fine details of the XANES spectrum offer insights into the atomic and molecular interactions, as well as the coordination and symmetry of atoms in different chemical environments.
This technique is widely used in various scientific fields, including chemistry, solid-state physics, and materials science. XANES helps researchers understand the properties and behavior of materials at the atomic level, making it an invaluable tool for investigating the characteristics of complex materials, catalysts, minerals, and biomolecules."""@en ;
                                          pmdco:definitionSource "ChatGPT 3.5"@en ;
                                          mo:abbreviation "XANES"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/mo/Xray_Absorption_Spectroscopy
mo:Xray_Absorption_Spectroscopy rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                rdfs:subClassOf mo:Xray_Mapping ;
                                rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/pmd/mo> ;
                                rdfs:label "Röntgenabsorptionsspektroskopie"@de ,
                                           "X-ray Absorption Spectroscopy"@en ;
                                skos:definition "X-ray Absorption Spectroscopy is a technique used to study the electronic and local structural properties of materials by analyzing the absorption of X-rays. It involves measuring how X-rays are absorbed by a sample at various energies, providing insights into the electronic states and chemical environments of specific elements."@en ;
                                pmdco:definitionSource "ChatGPT 3.5"@en ;
                                mo:abbreviation "XAS"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/mo/Xray_Analysis
mo:Xray_Analysis rdf:type owl:Class ;
                 rdfs:subClassOf pmdco:Analysing_Process ;
                 rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/pmd/mo> ;
                 rdfs:label "Röntgenanalyse"@de ,
                            "X-ray Analysis"@en ;
                 skos:definition "X-ray analysis is a technique used to investigate the composition and structure of materials by exposing them to X-rays. When X-rays interact with a material, they can be absorbed, scattered, or diffracted in ways that provide information about the material's internal arrangement of atoms and its elemental composition."@en ;
                 pmdco:definitionSource "ChatGPT 3.5"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/mo/Xray_Diffraction
mo:Xray_Diffraction rdf:type owl:Class ;
                    rdfs:subClassOf mo:Diffraktion ,
                                    [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                      owl:onProperty prov:used ;
                                      owl:someValuesFrom chips:Xray_Beam
                                    ] ,
                                    [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                      owl:onProperty prov:wasAssociatedWith ;
                                      owl:someValuesFrom chips:Xray_Beam
                                    ] ,
                                    [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                      owl:onProperty prov:wasAssociatedWith ;
                                      owl:someValuesFrom chips:Xray_Diffractometer
                                    ] ,
                                    [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                      owl:onProperty chips:measured ;
                                      owl:someValuesFrom chips:Lattice_Parameter
                                    ] ,
                                    [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                      owl:onProperty chips:measured ;
                                      owl:someValuesFrom chips:Morphology
                                    ] ,
                                    [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                      owl:onProperty chips:measured ;
                                      owl:someValuesFrom chips:Phase_Material
                                    ] ,
                                    [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                      owl:onProperty pmdco:belongsToProject ;
                                      owl:someValuesFrom [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                           owl:unionOf ( chips:Grand_Challenge_2
                                                                         chips:Grand_Challenge_3
                                                                         chips:Grand_Challenge_4
                                                                         chips:Grand_Challenge_5
                                                                         chips:Grand_Challenge_6
                                                                         chips:Grand_Challenge_7
                                                                       )
                                                         ]
                                    ] ;
                    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/pmd/mo> ;
                    rdfs:label "X-ray Diffraction"@en ;
                    skos:altLabel "Röntgenstrahlbeugung"@de ;
                    skos:definition "X-ray Diffraction is a technique that utilizes the diffraction of X-rays by crystals to determine their atomic arrangement and lattice structure. X-ray diffraction patterns are produced when X-rays strike a crystalline sample, and the resulting pattern provides information about the arrangement of atoms in the crystal lattice."@en ;
                    skos:prefLabel "Röntgenbeugung"@de ;
                    pmdco:definitionSource "ChatGPT 3.5"@en ;
                    mo:abbreviation "XRD"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/mo/Xray_Energy_Dispersive_Spectrometer
mo:Xray_Energy_Dispersive_Spectrometer rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                       rdfs:subClassOf mo:Spektrometer ,
                                                       [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                         owl:onProperty dcterms:isPartOf ;
                                                         owl:someValuesFrom pmdco:Elektronenmikroskop
                                                       ] ,
                                                       [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                         owl:onProperty prov:wasAssociateFor ;
                                                         owl:someValuesFrom mo:Energy_Dispersive_Xray_Spectroscopy
                                                       ] ,
                                                       [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                         owl:onProperty pmdco:hasFunction ;
                                                         owl:someValuesFrom [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                              owl:unionOf ( mo:Energy_Filter
                                                                                            mo:Image_Filter
                                                                                          )
                                                                            ]
                                                       ] ;
                                       rdfs:label "X-ray Energy Dispersive Spectrometer"@en ;
                                       skos:altLabel "Energy Dispersive Spectrometer"@en ;
                                       skos:definition "An X-ray energy dispersive spectrometer is a spectrometer that measures the energy distribution of characteristic X-rays emitted from a specimen under electron or photon bombardment, enabling rapid elemental identification and quantification."@en ;
                                       pmdco:abbreviation "EDS"@en ,
                                                          "XEDS"@en ;
                                       pmdco:definitionSource "claude-opus-4-6"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/mo/Xray_Fluorescence
mo:Xray_Fluorescence rdf:type owl:Class ;
                     rdfs:subClassOf chips:Fluorescence ,
                                     mo:Xray_Mapping ,
                                     [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                       owl:onProperty prov:generated ;
                                       owl:someValuesFrom chips:Xray_Fluorescence_Spectrum
                                     ] ;
                     rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/pmd/mo> ;
                     rdfs:label "Röntgenfluoreszenz"@de ,
                                "X-ray Fluorescence"@en ;
                     skos:definition "X-ray Fluorescence is a method used to determine the elemental composition of a sample by analyzing the X-rays emitted when the sample is exposed to high-energy X-rays. The X-rays emitted are characteristic of the elements present, allowing for quantitative analysis of the sample's elemental composition."@en ;
                     pmdco:definitionSource "ChatGPT 3.5"@en ;
                     mo:abbreviation "XRF"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/mo/Xray_Mapping
mo:Xray_Mapping rdf:type owl:Class ;
                rdfs:subClassOf mo:Xray_Analysis ;
                rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/pmd/mo> ;
                rdfs:label "Röntgen-Mapping"@de ,
                           "X-ray Mapping"@en ;
                skos:definition "X-ray mapping is a process that involves generating spatially resolved images of the distribution of specific elements within a sample. By collecting X-ray signals emitted or scattered from a sample at different points, an elemental map can be created, showing the varying concentrations of elements across the sample's surface."@en ;
                pmdco:definitionSource "ChatGPT 3.5"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/mo/Xray_Microanalysis
mo:Xray_Microanalysis rdf:type owl:Class ;
                      rdfs:subClassOf mo:Xray_Analysis ;
                      rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/pmd/mo> ;
                      rdfs:label "Röntgen-Mikroanalyse"@de ,
                                 "X-ray Microanalysis"@en ;
                      skos:definition "X-ray Microanalysis is a technique that combines microscopy and X-ray analysis to study the elemental composition of small regions within a sample. It involves focusing an electron or X-ray beam on a specific area of the sample and measuring the X-rays emitted from that area to determine the elemental composition."@en ;
                      pmdco:definitionSource "ChatGPT 3.5"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/pmd/mo/Xray_Photoelectron_Spectroscopy
mo:Xray_Photoelectron_Spectroscopy rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                   rdfs:subClassOf chips:Surface_Characterization_Process ,
                                                   mo:Xray_Mapping ,
                                                   [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                     owl:onProperty prov:generated ;
                                                     owl:someValuesFrom chips:Xray_Photoelectron_Spectrum
                                                   ] ,
                                                   [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                     owl:onProperty prov:used ;
                                                     owl:someValuesFrom chips:Xray_Beam
                                                   ] ,
                                                   [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                     owl:onProperty prov:wasAssociatedWith ;
                                                     owl:someValuesFrom chips:Xray_Photoelectron_Spectrometer
                                                   ] ,
                                                   [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                     owl:onProperty pmdco:belongsToProject ;
                                                     owl:someValuesFrom chips:Grand_Challenge_5
                                                   ] ;
                                   rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/pmd/mo> ;
                                   rdfs:label "Röntgenphotoelektronenspektroskopie"@de ,
                                              "X-ray Photoelectron Spectroscopy"@en ;
                                   skos:definition "X-ray Photoelectron Spectroscopy, also known as Electron Spectroscopy for Chemical Analysis (ESCA), is a technique used to study the surface chemistry of materials. XPS involves bombarding a sample's surface with X-rays to emit photoelectrons, which are then analyzed to determine the elemental composition and chemical states of the elements on the surface."@en ;
